Ladybird now draws every decoration line on SVG text in the element’s
text-decoration-style, as an outline the text’s fill and stroke paint.
Chrome 158 draws all four styles on SVG text too (Blink paints SVG text
decorations with the same decoration painter as HTML text, from
TextFragmentPainter), filled and stroked like the glyphs. Firefox 151
draws the styles as well, but thin, without the given thickness for a
wavy line. WebKit 26.5 draws only solid lines (and a double line):
SVGTextBoxPainter::paintDecorationWithStyle() adds a single rect to
the path it fills and strokes, whatever the style. Ladybird’s wavy
line is the zigzag our HTML text decorations use, rather than the
smoother wave that Chrome draws.
